WEBVTT

00:03.950 --> 00:06.870
Urin, where are you?

00:07.730 --> 00:10.150
Right here.

00:10.470 --> 00:12.040
Where?

00:12.040 --> 00:14.000
Hurry up and find me, Marin.

00:17.710 --> 00:19.330
Urin!

00:24.370 --> 00:28.470
Urin, it’s scary here.

00:28.470 --> 00:30.240
Can’t help it.

00:30.240 --> 00:31.410
Urin!

00:32.230 --> 00:32.590
Eh?

00:33.570 --> 00:34.800
I’m right here, Marin.

00:35.280 --> 00:37.930
Urin, I love yo–

00:43.300 --> 00:44.810
Marin is such a scaredy-cat.

00:44.810 --> 00:47.450
Sheesh, Urin!

00:52.240 --> 01:02.580
It would be great if we could stay together forever

01:03.630 --> 01:09.880
in a calm place, with only the sounds of waves –

01:09.880 --> 01:14.340
<i>a place where I can be relaxed.</i>

01:14.340 --> 01:21.600
<i>Where did it disappear to, though?</i>

01:21.600 --> 01:26.140
<i>Time has continued to move forward.</i>

01:26.750 --> 01:33.690
<i>The drop of water has fallen and disappeared.</i>

01:33.690 --> 01:40.090
<i>A tiny string of hope…</i>

01:40.090 --> 01:46.120
<i>In the sky, the flowers have blossomed.</i>

01:46.120 --> 01:51.790
<i>Can you hear the clear sound of breathing?</i>

01:51.790 --> 01:57.760
<i>The flower that brought me joy back then…</i>

01:57.760 --> 02:01.180
<i>Into the distant future,</i>

02:01.180 --> 02:13.690
I can be sure that I’ll be with you.

02:02.790 --> 02:03.920
Marin.

02:04.360 --> 02:05.900
Yes, Urin?

02:08.640 --> 02:10.310
Um…

02:31.250 --> 02:33.790
kimi to ireba

02:31.250 --> 02:33.790
If I’m with you -

02:33.790 --> 02:36.630
kimi to itara

02:33.790 --> 02:36.630
because I’m with you -

02:36.630 --> 02:41.260
kokoro ga yasuraku

02:36.630 --> 02:41.260
my heart is at ease.

02:42.220 --> 02:44.810
kimi mo soude

02:42.220 --> 02:44.810
Surely, you’re the same.

02:44.810 --> 02:50.350
kimi mo ima yasurakerute

02:44.810 --> 02:50.350
You’re at ease now, too.

02:51.400 --> 02:57.990
itekuretara ii noni

02:51.400 --> 02:57.990
If you can just admit it,

02:59.740 --> 03:03.320
sono mama

02:59.740 --> 03:03.320
for even time to forget us,

03:04.280 --> 03:17.460
jikan saemo wasuresouna kurai shizen dakara

03:04.280 --> 03:17.460
it’s only natural, at this rate.

03:18.210 --> 03:28.930
yubisaki kara koboreochiru violet wo yo

03:18.210 --> 03:28.930
Violet drops, falling slowly from our fingertips…

03:28.930 --> 03:35.820
chiisana yume egaite yukou

03:28.930 --> 03:35.820
“Let us follow that small dream with a smile!”

03:35.820 --> 03:41.740
futaride sasayaka na

03:35.820 --> 03:41.740
And just like that, we are happy

03:43.160 --> 03:47.370
kotoba ga ureshii

03:43.160 --> 03:47.370
over such trifling words

03:47.870 --> 03:52.080
somatteku sora

03:47.870 --> 03:52.080
that paint the sky.

04:15.540 --> 04:17.690
Urin…

04:18.030 --> 04:19.350
You’re awake.

04:18.070 --> 04:22.280
Hearts Seeking Help

04:19.350 --> 04:20.580
Are you okay?

04:21.290 --> 04:22.790
Where is this?

04:22.780 --> 04:25.490
You were caught in a current and ended up getting carried here.

04:25.490 --> 04:28.120
What a scary amount of power.

04:28.120 --> 04:31.160
I have to save Urin now.

04:31.160 --> 04:32.330
What?

04:32.330 --> 04:36.580
Wait! Your sister already rejected you.

04:36.580 --> 04:39.750
There won’t be a change, even if you go now.

04:39.750 --> 04:42.590
Impossible. This can’t be happening…

04:42.590 --> 04:43.970
I’m sure she’s waiting for me.

04:43.970 --> 04:47.720
Marin, I understand your feelings,
but there’s nothing we can do now.

04:47.730 --> 04:51.160
Why? Because I’m unable to transform into a priestess?

04:51.160 --> 04:51.890
Marin…

04:52.270 --> 04:54.730
Urin is my sister.

04:54.720 --> 04:58.590
Even if I’m not a priestess, my feelings will reach her.

04:58.590 --> 04:59.550
But just now…

04:59.570 --> 05:01.230
Kanon-chan, you don’t understand!

05:02.780 --> 05:06.780
Urin feels uneasy right now. She’s waiting for me to save her.

05:06.780 --> 05:08.070
I know that’s how it is!

05:08.090 --> 05:09.050
Marin!

05:10.240 --> 05:12.120
The one who feels uneasy is you, right?

05:14.160 --> 05:19.210
You’re unable to accept the thought of Urin leaving you, right?

05:24.490 --> 05:26.470
Why would Urin…

05:27.010 --> 05:32.060
It seems that when Urin released Sedona,

05:32.060 --> 05:36.390
Sedona’s evil possessed that ring,
and it controls her through the ring.

05:37.100 --> 05:38.020
The ring?

05:38.690 --> 05:42.110
By the way things have progressed, that seems to be the case.

05:42.110 --> 05:45.400
But wasn’t that originally Kanon-chan’s ring?

05:47.110 --> 05:49.370
If that damned ring didn’t exist…

05:53.540 --> 05:55.830
You don’t think saying “damned” is going too far?

05:55.830 --> 05:57.370
That’s the truth!

05:57.370 --> 05:59.460
Everyone, calm down.

05:59.460 --> 06:02.550
I’ll bring you guys some sea grapes later.

06:02.550 --> 06:07.970
Before that, Priestess of the Sky, you head on back to the Sky.

06:08.300 --> 06:12.050
You don’t have to say something like that, right?

06:13.640 --> 06:15.930
Kanon hasn’t come home yet.

06:15.930 --> 06:20.560
Is that so? This morning, I saw her swimming in the sea.

06:20.560 --> 06:23.360
It’s rare for Kanon to swim.

06:23.820 --> 06:27.990
If that’s the case, I think she is training.

06:27.990 --> 06:28.780
Training?

06:29.150 --> 06:32.120
Probably training with Matsumoto-san.

06:36.870 --> 06:38.660
How was it, Kojima-kun?

06:38.870 --> 06:41.170
She hasn’t come home yet.

06:41.170 --> 06:43.880
The waves are strong. I’m a little worried.

06:43.880 --> 06:47.590
Is that so? I wonder if Miyamori is all right.

06:47.590 --> 06:49.880
She hasn't answered her phone for a while now.

06:51.050 --> 06:54.010
That’s not good. If Miyamori dies like this,

06:54.010 --> 06:57.220
she will forever remain in Kojima-kun’s memory.

06:57.210 --> 06:58.850
And wearing a school swimsuit, to boot!

06:59.910 --> 07:00.980
I’m dying!

07:00.980 --> 07:03.610
Damn you, Miyamori! I won’t forgive you!

07:05.070 --> 07:06.290
She’s not picking up.

07:06.280 --> 07:09.110
Why don’t we look around some more?

07:09.700 --> 07:10.900
Then, let’s…

07:10.900 --> 07:11.990
Go together!

07:10.900 --> 07:11.990
Split up.

07:12.870 --> 07:15.660
Um, split up, you say?

07:15.660 --> 07:18.080
Ooshima, you can go and look around the shrine.

07:18.080 --> 07:20.960
I’ll go over the beach again.

07:29.710 --> 07:31.070
I’m sorry.

07:32.090 --> 07:36.560
Marin is very worried about Urin.
That’s why she said something like that.

07:37.060 --> 07:40.180
No worries, I understand. They are sisters, after all.

07:40.180 --> 07:41.730
Sisters? Well…

07:42.850 --> 07:45.270
We are different from Sky people.

07:45.270 --> 07:48.530
After we’re born, we get raised in a seashell,

07:48.530 --> 07:51.200
so we know neither our parents nor siblings.

07:52.450 --> 07:57.530
But Marin and Urin were raised in a rare, pure white shell.

07:58.580 --> 08:01.580
The elder turtle said they have the blood of the priestess.

08:02.120 --> 08:03.040
That’s correct.

08:03.870 --> 08:07.000
It’s somewhat different from what you’d call being siblings, though.

08:07.920 --> 08:12.760
But they’ve gotten along ever since they met,

08:12.760 --> 08:15.590
so I guess that makes them siblings.

08:20.060 --> 08:21.770
Nice to meet you!

08:30.690 --> 08:33.240
For now, we’ll just wait for our chance.

08:33.240 --> 08:35.860
First, we need to restore ourselves.

08:35.860 --> 08:38.700
Fighting Sedona comes later.

08:38.700 --> 08:41.080
Marin, I picked some sea grapes.

08:43.830 --> 08:46.130
Urin is waiting…

08:46.130 --> 08:47.790
Sea grapes?

08:48.250 --> 08:49.800
I have to go and find her.

08:50.460 --> 08:55.720
She is waiting for me, just like that time…

08:56.300 --> 08:57.680
That time?

08:58.640 --> 09:04.940
Right, when they were little, Marin, Urin, Sam and I went to see the coral reef.

09:06.020 --> 09:08.770
It was Urin’s first time,

09:08.770 --> 09:11.900
so we went to an especially distant reef.

09:11.900 --> 09:14.530
Halfway there, Urin got separated from us.

09:23.250 --> 09:26.540
Urin! Urin!

09:31.340 --> 09:33.920
Warin and I were also looking for her,

09:34.260 --> 09:38.340
but the coral reef was too big, and we couldn’t find her.

09:53.780 --> 09:54.900
Marin!

09:56.700 --> 09:57.910
What’s wrong?

09:57.910 --> 10:00.620
I just heard Urin’s voice.

10:01.090 --> 10:03.150
Wait, Marin!

10:07.840 --> 10:09.050
Urin!

10:10.170 --> 10:11.500
Marin!

10:11.830 --> 10:13.170
I found you!

10:15.830 --> 10:17.460
Marin!

10:17.460 --> 10:19.180
Urin, were you scared?

10:20.800 --> 10:22.930
It’s all right now.

10:47.030 --> 10:48.250
It started.

10:49.460 --> 10:54.040
Wow, it’s so beautiful.

10:56.540 --> 10:57.770
Onee-chan…

10:59.810 --> 11:01.290
Onee-chan.

11:03.140 --> 11:05.520
Urin, I love you!

11:07.100 --> 11:12.400
That was the first time Urin called Marin her sister.

11:13.650 --> 11:16.690
Those two really did become siblings.

11:17.860 --> 11:19.570
Is that so?

11:23.070 --> 11:24.240
Urin…

11:30.790 --> 11:32.670
Just a little longer.

11:32.690 --> 11:37.250
If I become stronger, Onee-chan will pick me up.

11:47.010 --> 11:49.560
Somehow, the taste is different.

11:49.560 --> 11:51.020
I’m home.

11:51.020 --> 11:52.980
Welcome home.

11:53.310 --> 11:55.360
You really went into the sea, huh?

11:57.320 --> 11:59.240
Guess who just came over.

12:00.330 --> 12:01.800
It was Kojima-kun.

12:02.730 --> 12:03.450
Kojima?

12:03.780 --> 12:08.240
He was really worried about you, panicking about you drowning…

12:08.240 --> 12:11.000
Did you guys get back together?

12:11.000 --> 12:12.920
A lot of things happened.

12:13.620 --> 12:16.540
What did you do?!
You took that from the barrel of pickles!

12:16.540 --> 12:18.340
No wonder the flavor of the pickles changed!

12:18.340 --> 12:19.390
Give it back!

12:19.390 --> 12:20.170
Not yet.

12:24.590 --> 12:26.390
Wait, Priestess of the Sea!

12:26.890 --> 12:28.930
What do you intend to do?

12:28.930 --> 12:30.810
I want to go and pick up Urin,

12:30.810 --> 12:33.810
and then go to the coral reef together.

12:34.560 --> 12:37.480
Right, if she can recall that memory,

12:37.480 --> 12:38.730
she’ll come back for sure.

12:39.520 --> 12:43.650
It’s too dangerous… Makes me nervous.

12:52.830 --> 12:57.670
Eh? He was that worried about me?

12:58.960 --> 13:01.050
Well, what should I tell him?

13:01.880 --> 13:07.470
I should at least tell him I’m safe…

13:08.650 --> 13:11.140
If that damned ring didn’t exist…

13:12.470 --> 13:16.440
What about it? It doesn’t have anything to do with Kojima.

13:17.400 --> 13:19.730
If I hadn’t thrown it away…

13:20.650 --> 13:23.110
But I was the one who got dumped.

13:25.140 --> 13:26.320
Who?

13:26.930 --> 13:27.350
Hello?

13:27.360 --> 13:29.570
Ah! She picked up!

13:30.160 --> 13:32.290
This has become
a problem instead...

13:30.740 --> 13:31.840
I hung up.

13:36.180 --> 13:36.560
Yeah?

13:36.540 --> 13:38.750
Don’t die yet, school swimsuit girl!

13:46.050 --> 13:47.340
I want to die.

13:47.340 --> 13:52.260
What’s that? We were worried that you really did die!

13:52.260 --> 13:53.720
Huh? You were?

13:53.720 --> 13:57.980
Kojima-kun was. Well, I was too, but for a different reason.

13:58.770 --> 14:00.480
Thank you for worrying about me.

14:00.480 --> 14:01.980
What are you, stupid?

14:05.530 --> 14:10.240
I say, if you want to dump Kojima-kun, then do it clearly.

14:13.330 --> 14:16.660
My ass! Did you even listen to me?!

14:15.160 --> 14:16.660
Wait a minute, Ooshima.

14:16.660 --> 14:18.580
I was the one who got dumped.

14:21.310 --> 14:23.880
Plus, aren’t you and Kojima dating?

14:27.050 --> 14:30.140
If that’s how things are, then I won’t need to call you out.

14:30.140 --> 14:35.140
It seemed like the time we spent together
and the frequency of messaging decreased, though.

14:35.430 --> 14:38.730
Felt like I was forcing myself to go out with him.

14:39.390 --> 14:42.690
But heck, my ranking dropped from the last exam.

14:44.150 --> 14:47.570
Your ranking went up, didn’t it?

14:49.320 --> 14:52.070
Well, I guess we shouldn’t force ourselves.

14:52.070 --> 14:52.740
Just be frank.

14:54.330 --> 14:57.120
Just say it. You don’t have to keep acting.

14:57.910 --> 15:00.920
You’re trying to say your rank dropped because of me, right?

15:00.920 --> 15:03.170
Wait a minute, I didn’t say that!

15:03.170 --> 15:05.630
Oh, really? Why don’t you just say so?

15:05.630 --> 15:08.380
I got used to hearing that, anyway.

15:11.470 --> 15:12.970
Why…

15:14.210 --> 15:16.990
It’s up to you if you want to dump me.

15:21.770 --> 15:24.400
YOU IDIOT!

15:26.070 --> 15:30.400
Really, why did Kojima-kun want this dumb girl?!

15:30.400 --> 15:32.990
Stupid! Is everyone an idiot?!

15:32.990 --> 15:35.240
But you guys watched the fireworks together.

15:35.240 --> 15:38.660
We did, and I purposely picked a place where you would see us.

15:41.870 --> 15:46.920
But all he did was talk about you.

15:46.920 --> 15:53.010
Even when choosing the ring –
and yes, it was me who went with him…

15:53.010 --> 15:59.430
He didn’t have to be so happy choosing it when I was right there…

15:59.880 --> 16:02.640
Didn’t you choose that ring?

16:02.640 --> 16:06.110
I lied! Of course I didn’t! You actually believed that?!

16:07.320 --> 16:12.280
It it’d been me, I would’ve picked the worst, ugliest ring possible!

16:10.360 --> 16:12.280
Of course...

16:15.490 --> 16:19.660
This fits Miyamori pretty well, don’t you think?

16:19.660 --> 16:21.870
Yeah, I think so, too.

16:26.290 --> 16:28.800
I sure hope Miyamori will be glad to accept this…

16:28.800 --> 16:30.840
I’m sure she will be.

16:32.510 --> 16:34.130
Thank you.

16:36.680 --> 16:38.310
Kojima was…

16:43.640 --> 16:46.860
Here. I hope you like it.

16:49.110 --> 16:50.650
A ring?

17:01.200 --> 17:07.710
But I really think his heart is just as beautiful as this gift.

17:08.760 --> 17:11.800
So, it was me all along.

17:11.800 --> 17:16.130
It was me who made myself feel uneasy,
thinking that I was getting dumped by him.

17:16.130 --> 17:18.850
You’re not saying you still like him, right?

17:22.270 --> 17:25.100
Are you for real? Are you kidding me?!

17:26.190 --> 17:28.730
Ooshima! Are you all right?

17:30.320 --> 17:31.610
Why…

17:34.230 --> 17:37.240
Why can’t it be me?

17:37.240 --> 17:39.800
Why does it have to be you?

17:39.780 --> 17:43.450
I like Kojima-kun too…

17:43.440 --> 17:45.380
Ooshima…

17:45.370 --> 17:49.580
Why do I have to suffer so much because of you?

17:50.170 --> 17:54.380
I’ve never liked someone this much before.

17:54.970 --> 17:56.880
Why?

17:57.630 --> 18:02.930
Why do I have to suffer, even though I like him?

18:07.340 --> 18:09.000
I’ve said too much.

18:10.650 --> 18:12.360
Why are you crying?!

18:13.690 --> 18:18.150
I was thinking, this is how it feels like to like someone.

18:18.570 --> 18:20.780
You’re too noisy!

18:25.910 --> 18:28.570
School swimsuit girl turned into salt water girl.

18:28.210 --> 18:29.920
Even though
I did, too.

18:30.580 --> 18:35.380
I’ll help you tell Kojima-kun that the annoying person is okay now.

18:36.340 --> 18:37.340
Thank you.

18:38.970 --> 18:41.010
I won’t lose.

18:59.780 --> 19:04.240
What is this? It is full of dark energy here.

19:04.260 --> 19:06.200
Urin is in there.

19:06.660 --> 19:07.750
Urin!

19:09.160 --> 19:11.460
Urin, I came to pick you up!

19:11.460 --> 19:12.750
Let’s go and see the coral reef!

19:14.840 --> 19:17.170
Onee-chan came.

19:17.170 --> 19:18.420
Urin!

19:20.840 --> 19:22.010
What is this?

19:33.090 --> 19:35.110
Marin, I’ll come save you now.

19:37.410 --> 19:38.390
Warin.

19:39.110 --> 19:41.860
I didn’t see you back there, so I knew you’d be here.

19:41.860 --> 19:43.780
Really, what are you thinking?

19:48.380 --> 19:49.580
Warin!

19:54.160 --> 19:54.870
Warin!

20:01.140 --> 20:02.420
Keep it up!

20:08.440 --> 20:10.270
Onee-chan.

20:15.690 --> 20:17.770
Are you all right, Marin?

20:17.770 --> 20:19.820
Yeah. Thanks.

20:20.360 --> 20:24.530
The evil power is increasing in there.

20:24.530 --> 20:26.070
Don’t approach it so carelessly.

20:26.760 --> 20:27.910
But Urin…

20:27.910 --> 20:28.690
Idiot!

20:30.500 --> 20:32.610
Stop it already!

20:33.620 --> 20:37.210
Why don’t you think about how to get your priestess powers back?

20:37.810 --> 20:42.060
If you want to save Urin, isn’t that the only way?

20:42.060 --> 20:46.140
Even if you say so, I don’t know what to do.

20:46.430 --> 20:52.770
Since the day of the solar eclipse, the Priestess of the Sea’s heart has been covered by darkness.

20:52.760 --> 20:54.770
What should we do?

20:57.000 --> 20:59.170
Go to Kanon.

20:59.820 --> 21:01.990
To Kanon-chan?

21:02.570 --> 21:06.030
Even though darkness has clouded her heart from the start,

21:06.030 --> 21:07.950
she can still transform into a priestess.

21:08.580 --> 21:13.710
She’s the one who will show you how to get that power back.

21:14.620 --> 21:17.130
Warin has a point.

21:17.130 --> 21:19.590
But Kanon-chan is…

21:19.590 --> 21:22.460
Marin still hates Kanon?

21:25.160 --> 21:26.930
Then, why not?

21:27.720 --> 21:32.100
The energetic and optimistic girl – that’s the Marin I like.

21:32.470 --> 21:36.640
Don’t worry. You’ll get your priestess powers back for sure.

21:42.190 --> 21:44.980
The ones you miss are gone.

21:45.700 --> 21:49.740
Why did they leave, when they’d finally gotten here?

21:49.730 --> 21:52.220
No one will come again.

21:52.200 --> 21:54.750
But I’m right here.

21:54.770 --> 21:56.920
No one will ever come again.

21:57.290 --> 21:59.460
No one will come again?

21:59.460 --> 22:02.910
Loneliness will bring sorrow.

22:02.910 --> 22:04.820
What should I do?

22:04.820 --> 22:06.850
I don’t want to be alone.

22:06.850 --> 22:09.850
No one should be forgiven.

22:11.220 --> 22:12.640
No one.

22:26.610 --> 22:31.530
hikari no yurikago

22:26.610 --> 22:31.530
Within a droplet of water,

22:31.950 --> 22:35.080
shizuku no naka ni

22:31.950 --> 22:35.080
a cradle of light

22:35.410 --> 22:38.330
tojikometara

22:35.410 --> 22:38.330
is trapped.

22:38.330 --> 22:43.500
mizu no iro ni naru

22:38.330 --> 22:43.500
And so, it colors the water.

22:43.920 --> 22:47.130
mimi wo sumashite

22:43.920 --> 22:47.130
Clear your ears

22:47.130 --> 22:49.800
eien e

22:47.130 --> 22:49.720
to eternity.

22:49.800 --> 22:55.100
hitori de yume no ato

22:49.880 --> 22:55.100
Beyond a lonely dream,

22:55.100 --> 23:00.440
tsunaide yukeba

22:55.100 --> 23:00.440
if one connects with another,

23:01.150 --> 23:07.030
sotto kurikaesu kagayaki

23:01.150 --> 23:07.030
the repeating, soft shine

23:07.440 --> 23:12.070
warattemo attete

23:07.440 --> 23:12.070
meets and smiles,

23:12.070 --> 23:19.250
mou sukoshide kokoro ga todoku kara

23:12.070 --> 23:19.250
and with just a little more, the hearts have been reached.

23:19.250 --> 23:23.960
toumeina inori de

23:19.250 --> 23:23.840
With a transparent prayer,

23:23.960 --> 23:33.300
yasashiikuchikamu wo tsutsumuyo

23:23.960 --> 23:33.300
concealed within a gentle mouth.

23:35.540 --> 23:38.180
Did you know? Cuttlefish can transform.

23:38.180 --> 23:39.950
Its appearance in the day is different from the night.

23:39.930 --> 23:42.520
I change a little during nighttime too.

23:42.910 --> 23:43.940
I don’t understand.

23:43.940 --> 23:45.520
Next time, Episode 9:

23:45.190 --> 23:49.940
Loving Hearts

23:45.520 --> 23:46.980
Loving Hearts.

23:47.000 --> 23:49.940
I love everyone!
